# GitHub's SSH host keys, pinned: CI writes these into known_hosts and never
# asks the network for them. `ssh-keyscan github.com` at run time failed a
# Windows job before it built anything when the runner's DNS blipped
# ("getaddrinfo github.com: No such host is known"), and it trusts whatever
# answers on port 22.
#
# Source: GitHub's documentation, "GitHub's SSH key fingerprints",
# https://docs.github.com/en/authentication/keeping-your-account-and-data-secure/githubs-ssh-key-fingerprints
# (the same keys and fingerprints as "ssh_keys" and "ssh_key_fingerprints"
# in https://api.github.com/meta). Checked against both on 2026-11-17.
#
# The fingerprints GitHub publishes for them. github-host-keys.tests.sh checks
# each key line below against these, offline; github-host-keys-live.yml checks
# both against GitHub itself, weekly and on a change to this file.
# fingerprint SHA256:+DiY3wvvV6TuJJhbpZisF/zLDA0zPMSvHdkr4UvCOqU ED25519
# fingerprint SHA256:p2QAMXNIC1TJYWeIOttrVc98/R1BUFWu3/LiyKgUfQM ECDSA
# fingerprint SHA256:uNiVztksCsDhcc0u9e8BujQXVUpKZIDTMczCvj3tD2s RSA
#
# Read by .github/scripts/windows/setup-git-isolation.ps1 and the
# setup-private-parsers action. prepare_and_run.yml's inline "Setup per-job
# git isolation" step runs before the checkout, so it carries a copy of the
# key lines. When GitHub changes a key, change the key line, its fingerprint
# line and that copy; github-host-keys.tests.sh fails until all three agree.
